<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! realm.cabal.clocks ~ the capture-clock: who feeds, how deep, no verdict

`lares cabal clock --realm <id>` reads the maintainers this replica has synced, each slot's epoch, the spread and the leading edge, and sets the realm's standing beside it (one face a visit, several many-faces). It draws no capture verdict; a realm nobody here has synced reads the same as an unfed one.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ clock

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`clock` params=`realm/0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef ~ read who feeds the realm`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ realm

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`realm` params=`takes/doc-id needs/required ~ the cabal-realm doc id, 64 hex`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ reads this replica's realm doc; writes nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage · store-refused

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[realm.cabal.clocks realm/0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef]] ~ --realm expects a 64-hex cabal-realm doc id`>>
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`store-refused` params=`~ the store door refused, or no vessel answers; the line names why`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

